The data is stored in JSON format and organized into 5-minute intervals. The LiDAR object list is recorded at 10 Hz (10 frames per second).

Each frame contains a timestamp and a list of detected objects with the following information:

- frame_timestamp: Timestamp of the frame (seconds and nanosec).
- timestamp_local: Local date and time of the frame.
- objects: List of detected objects in the frame.
  - track_id: Unique ID assigned to a tracked object.
  - class_name: Type of object (e.g., Car, Pedestrian).
  - score: Detection confidence score.
  - bounding_box:
    - position (x, y, z): 3D position of the object.
    - yaw: Orientation of the object.
    - scale (x, y, z): Object dimensions (length, width, height).
  - velocity (x, y): Object velocity along the x and y axes.

The same object can appear in multiple consecutive frames with its track_id, allowing its movement to be tracked over time.
